The reference xfoil-python that xfoil_c reproduces and its tests compare against: changes to
https://github.com/daniel-de-vries/xfoil-python (master, commit 5c8c4ff, 2019). Apply in a checkout with
    git apply xfoil-python.patch
then build it (pip install .) and copy the library into xfoil/ if pip did not (see the xfoil_c README, "Tests").

- api.f90 / xfoil.py: double precision at the library boundary (upstream passes float32); a() and cl() also
  return the transition points xtr_top, xtr_bot; get_cp_distribution() returns x, y, cp; set_mach also sets
  MINF1. The library is loaded once (upstream loads a temporary copy per XFoil instance, so its instances have
  separate state; here they share one).
- CMakeLists.txt / setup.py / pyproject.toml: library name xfoil_fortran; flags -O2 -fdefault-real-8
  -fno-range-check -fno-tree-vectorize (no auto-vectorisation, so no glibc vector math, which differs in the
  last bits; needed for bit-identical comparison); setuptools build backend.
- test.py: the 6 return values; test_a's cp re-baselined to -5.5077 for current gfortran (upstream -5.5766).

